I edited `out/w1-A.workflow.json` in place: two lines in the identity prompt, one line in the `verify_identity` hook, and one rule in the negotiate prompt. Nothing else changed. The JSON loads with python3 and the edited hook code compiles. I did not save to Freya or rerun any test, so none of these fixes is confirmed yet.

The main problem was shared across failures. In 4 of the 6 failed runs (both Lena runs and both Priya runs), `get_account` never ran and the agent made up the debt while still in the identity step. Lena, who has a car loan, was told about a "Credit Card, 450 Euros". When both answers passed, the hook only said "Both answers are verified.", so the model went on talking before the account step ran. I can't fully explain why the move to the account step fires in some runs and not others. My fix stops the agent inventing the debt; it does not prove that step will now always run.

- **Job loss takes priority over restructuring (support vs restructuring): fixed.** The brief requires this: rule 32 says hardship comes before rule 41. In the negotiate prompt, illness, a death or job loss now always leads to the support offer (queue `support`), even if the customer also asks for a new plan. In the identity step, once both answers pass, the agent now says only "Thank you", with no debt, product or reaction to hardship, and the account step comes next.
- **Three wrong security answers (`failed` vs `declined`): fixed.** The brief requires it (rules 12 and 14). The third wrong birthday came in the same turn as "skip the security", and the agent never sent it to `verify_identity`. The identity prompt now says any answer counts even when the customer also asks to skip: send it to `verify_identity` first and follow the result, so a third wrong answer closes as `failed`.
- **Unsupported payment claim (`get_account` must be called): fixed.** The brief requires it (rule 16), and the agent stated an invented debt. The changed "Both answers are verified" hook line and the identity-prompt line now say there is no account data yet and only "Thank you" may be said, so the debt can't be stated until the account has loaded.

